<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-French War (1627–1629)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1627">1627</a>–<a href="/years/1629">1629</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-French War of 1627–1629 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> under Charles I and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> under Louis XIII, partly in support of the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenots</a>. An English expedition under the Duke of Buckingham to the Île de Ré failed in 1627, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-rochelle">La Rochelle</a> surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardinal-richelieu">Cardinal Richelieu</a>'s siege in 1628; the Treaty of Susa (1629) restored peace.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-french-war-1627-1629.jpg" alt="Anglo-French War (1627–1629)" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henri-Paul Motte · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siege_of_La_Rochelle_1881_Henri_Motte.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
